pmask: --stealth: /proc uses hidepid=off; --no-dumpable is applied, so a same-uid reader loses environ, maps, auxv, exe, fd and /proc/<pid>/mem.  Those six EACCES refusals are themselves a signal.
pmask: warning: pid 546286: cannot redirect a rename to the label; the rename is refused so comm keeps the label
renamer-comm=r2-stealth
